1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

3
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

4
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,546
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

6
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:04,356
[Youjin] What are you
thinking about right now?

7
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:12,197
What are you thinking about?

8
00:01:12,864 --> 00:01:14,700
[hesitating] I wasn't thinking
about anything.

9
00:01:16,827 --> 00:01:18,745
Wait, you feel kind of warm.

10
00:01:18,829 --> 00:01:19,830
[Minjae] Hmm?

11
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:22,457
No, I'm not.

12
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:24,167
[Youjin] Let me see.

13
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,170
I think you have a bit of a fever.

14
00:01:28,589 --> 00:01:31,842
-That's because I have a bit of a cold.
-[Youjin] Yeah.

15
00:01:32,384 --> 00:01:33,927
I just need to take medicine and...

16
00:01:34,011 --> 00:01:35,429
Yeah, I just need to take meds.

17
00:01:36,388 --> 00:01:39,016
Then eat the porridge, take your meds,
and get some sleep.

18
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:40,100
Hold on a second.

19
00:01:40,809 --> 00:01:41,810
[Minjae] Okay.

20
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:45,147
FINAL EPISODE

21
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:48,817
[Youjin] Do you have a bowl for this?

22
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:50,068
-A bowl?
-[Youjin] Yes.

23
00:01:50,152 --> 00:01:51,737
[Minjae] A bowl... Right.

24
00:01:54,906 --> 00:01:56,366
I've got two here.

25
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:57,784
[Youjin] Just one is enough.

26
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:00,537
Why? Aren't you going to eat?

27
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:01,621
[Youjin] No, I'm good.

28
00:02:03,749 --> 00:02:05,625
But... Why not?

29
00:02:05,709 --> 00:02:06,960
Let's eat together.

30
00:02:07,711 --> 00:02:08,962
-Hmm?
-[Youjin] Mmm-mmm.

31
00:02:10,172 --> 00:02:12,549
It's still warm.
I don't think we need to heat it up.

32
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:16,678
One moment.

33
00:02:24,019 --> 00:02:25,145
[Minjae] Thank you.

34
00:02:25,228 --> 00:02:26,897
[Youjin] You need
the side dishes too, right?

35
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:31,526
Side dishes? Side dishes...

36
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:34,446
There's kimchi...

37
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:36,573
[Youjin] Kimchi would be too spicy
for you right now.

38
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:40,577
Do you have a sauce dish?

39
00:02:40,661 --> 00:02:43,372
[Minjae] A sauce dish? Yeah. Hold on.

40
00:02:44,206 --> 00:02:45,666
A small dish...

41
00:02:47,292 --> 00:02:48,752
This. I have this one.

42
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:50,170
[Youjin] Yeah, this one will do.

43
00:02:52,172 --> 00:02:53,382
You can sit down.

44
00:02:53,465 --> 00:02:54,466
[Minjae] Okay.

45
00:03:04,434 --> 00:03:05,435
[Youjin] Here.

46
00:03:07,562 --> 00:03:08,772
Eat up.

47
00:03:08,855 --> 00:03:09,856
[Minjae] Okay.

48
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:12,818
[Youjin] If it's too bland,
add some soy sauce.

49
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:14,903
[Minjae] Okay.

50
00:03:20,826 --> 00:03:22,452
Mmm! Mmm.

51
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:25,122
[Youjin] Hmm.

52
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:28,166
But it's probably not bland.

53
00:03:30,794 --> 00:03:34,297
I was bawling my eyes out when I made it.

54
00:03:35,424 --> 00:03:38,009
That porridge has at least
two bowls of my tears in it,

55
00:03:38,093 --> 00:03:40,679
so there's no way it's bland.
It might even be too salty.

56
00:03:45,642 --> 00:03:50,564
Did you cry because you were so worried
and sad when you heard I was sick?

57
00:03:54,234 --> 00:03:55,360
Why are you laughing?

58
00:03:56,111 --> 00:03:57,404
Is this funny to you?

59
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:11,918
It's not salty.

60
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:14,171
It's sweet.

61
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:17,716
I'm telling the truth.

62
00:04:19,217 --> 00:04:20,302
Try it.

63
00:04:21,011 --> 00:04:23,096
It's sweet. It's really delicious.

64
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:24,181
Here.

65
00:04:24,723 --> 00:04:26,558
Come on, just try a bite. Come on.

66
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:28,727
-[Youjin sighs]
-[Minjae] Come on.

67
00:04:38,862 --> 00:04:41,656
If you thought I forgave it all,
you're wrong.

68
00:04:43,784 --> 00:04:45,786
We're not back together.

69
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:48,622
We're not?

70
00:04:48,705 --> 00:04:50,165
[Youjin] Of course not.

71
00:04:50,248 --> 00:04:54,211
I'm super petty, okay?
And I hold grudges forever.

72
00:04:54,294 --> 00:04:56,546
So don't get the wrong idea.

73
00:04:58,215 --> 00:04:59,216
[Minjae] Okay.

74
00:05:05,514 --> 00:05:06,723
[Youjin] What?

75
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:11,311
I don't want to eat anymore.

76
00:05:16,066 --> 00:05:18,193
Well, we can't see each other.

77
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:21,404
We can't do that.

78
00:05:23,281 --> 00:05:25,617
But we can talk on the phone at night.

79
00:05:26,952 --> 00:05:27,953
On the phone?

80
00:05:28,036 --> 00:05:29,037
[Youjin] Yeah.

81
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,581
If you call me at night, I'll answer.

82
00:05:35,252 --> 00:05:36,586
So calling me is okay.

83
00:05:37,671 --> 00:05:40,715
And thinking about me before going to bed.
You can do that too.

84
00:05:43,134 --> 00:05:46,471
And when you wake up in the morning,
you can think about me first thing.

85
00:05:46,555 --> 00:05:48,265
That's okay too. You can do that.

86
00:05:50,559 --> 00:05:53,395
And you can think about me all day.

87
00:05:53,478 --> 00:05:57,566
And like me. Like me like crazy.

88
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:01,444
Well, that one's kind of tricky, actually.

89
00:06:02,279 --> 00:06:03,905
No. Actually, you can do that.

90
00:06:06,241 --> 00:06:07,325
-[Minjae] Okay.
-[Youjin] All right.

91
00:06:07,951 --> 00:06:09,536
Will you eat that porridge now?

92
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:14,249
[Minjae] Huh? Yeah.

93
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:21,381
But we can't get back together
or start dating again.

94
00:06:26,136 --> 00:06:28,096
We can't do that?

95
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:29,180
[Youjin] No.

96
00:06:30,682 --> 00:06:33,059
Some things you can,
some things you can't.

97
00:06:33,143 --> 00:06:35,270
Sometimes this, sometimes that.

98
00:06:35,353 --> 00:06:36,479
Complicated, isn't it?

99
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:41,651
-[Minjae sighs]
-[Youjin chuckles softly]

100
00:06:41,735 --> 00:06:43,028
You're so cute.

101
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:47,949
Hang on a second.

102
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:53,872
It's Mom. I should head home.

103
00:06:54,539 --> 00:06:56,249
-[Minjae] Okay.
-[Youjin] I'm sorry.

104
00:06:56,333 --> 00:06:59,377
[Minjae] No worries.
I'll call you a taxi. One second.

105
00:06:59,461 --> 00:07:02,464
[Youjin] Don't.
I can just take a bus home. It's okay.

106
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:04,841
Then let me walk you to the bus stop.

107
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:06,926
The bus stop is right around the corner.

108
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:08,345
I can go by myself.

109
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:09,471
[Minjae] But...

110
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:12,223
Finish the porridge, take your meds,
and get some rest.

111
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:13,308
I'll call you.

112
00:07:13,391 --> 00:07:15,268
[Minjae] But... No, wait. Wait.

113
00:07:15,352 --> 00:07:17,062
Wait right there.

114
00:07:17,145 --> 00:07:18,271
Give me one second.

115
00:07:19,481 --> 00:07:21,191
-Now...
-[door lock beeps]

116
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:30,700
Oh.

117
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:37,582
Youjin.

118
00:08:03,692 --> 00:08:05,151
-[door closes]
-[door lock beeps]

119
00:08:19,958 --> 00:08:20,959
Where are you?

120
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:23,336
Hey, I said I'd walk you to the bus stop.

121
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:26,089
You don't need to. I said I'm okay.

122
00:08:27,006 --> 00:08:28,007
Yeah.

123
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:31,594
Ah. I'm almost there already.

124
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:35,348
Yeah. I'm already at the bus stop.

125
00:08:36,558 --> 00:08:37,559
Yeah.

126
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:39,769
I'll call you when I get home.

127
00:09:18,892 --> 00:09:19,893
-[Minjae] Hello.
-[digital beeps]

128
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,232
-[Youjin] Huh?
-[Minjae groans]

129
00:09:27,275 --> 00:09:28,443
Man, it's cold.

130
00:09:29,778 --> 00:09:31,196
When did you get here?

131
00:09:44,334 --> 00:09:45,502
It's cold, isn't it?

132
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:46,586
[Minjae] Yeah.

133
00:09:54,761 --> 00:09:56,179
Do you want to listen to music?

134
00:09:56,971 --> 00:09:58,098
Yeah, I'd love to.

135
00:10:08,358 --> 00:10:09,526
Is this the right side?

136
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:12,362
Like this. There.

137
00:10:25,834 --> 00:10:26,835
Me?

138
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:26,102
[Minjae] Go on in.

139
00:11:26,186 --> 00:11:27,187
[Youjin] Okay.

140
00:11:27,270 --> 00:11:28,271
[Minjae] Make sure to eat.

141
00:11:29,063 --> 00:11:30,481
Bye. I'll call you.

142
00:11:30,565 --> 00:11:31,566
[Minjae] Bye.

143
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:42,118
-It's cold. Go.
-[Minjae] No, it's not cold.

144
00:11:42,202 --> 00:11:43,328
I'll watch you head in.

145
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:46,873
-Bye.
-[Minjae] Go.

146
00:11:54,672 --> 00:11:55,924
-[Youjin mouthing] Go.
-[Minjae mouthing] Go.

147
00:12:47,350 --> 00:12:49,519
Mom, is Youjin home?

148
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:52,021
Yeah. She just got home. Why?

149
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:54,399
[Youseong] What do you mean, why?

150
00:12:54,482 --> 00:12:55,692
[loudly] Hey, Lim Youjin!

151
00:12:56,734 --> 00:12:58,987
It's your day off,

152
00:12:59,070 --> 00:13:01,155
and you can't even stay home for once?

153
00:13:01,239 --> 00:13:04,534
You could at least run some errands
for Mom and help her out a little.

154
00:13:04,617 --> 00:13:05,952
She's got a lot on her plate.

155
00:13:06,035 --> 00:13:07,036
Come on.

156
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,914
You ran one errand,
and you're making a big deal out of it?

157
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:14,210
[Youseong] Mom, I'm not saying this
because I ran one errand.

158
00:13:14,294 --> 00:13:15,712
I'm telling the truth.

159
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:17,171
Hey, Youjin.

160
00:13:17,255 --> 00:13:18,631
Come on, am I wrong?

161
00:13:18,715 --> 00:13:21,050
Didn't you bring
the porridge container back home?

162
00:13:21,134 --> 00:13:23,761
I mean, the thermos
you put the porridge in earlier.

163
00:13:23,845 --> 00:13:26,222
I forgot. [clears throat]
I'll make sure to get it back.

164
00:13:26,306 --> 00:13:27,307
[Miyoung] Okay.

165
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:28,933
Porridge?

166
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:35,481
Youjin's friend is sick, so she made
some porridge and went over to see her.

167
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:37,734
Man, she didn't even get to rest
on her day off.

168
00:13:38,568 --> 00:13:39,610
Her friend?

169
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:43,156
Hey, who is this friend
you even made porridge for?

170
00:13:45,158 --> 00:13:48,161
Who did you make the porridge for?
I said, who is it?

171
00:13:48,244 --> 00:13:49,245
Who is this friend?

172
00:13:49,328 --> 00:13:51,164
Jeez, it's Subin.

173
00:13:52,707 --> 00:13:54,417
Subin caught a cold.

174
00:13:55,835 --> 00:13:58,796
What? Subin caught a cold?

175
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:00,381
[Miyoung] Yeah, apparently.

176
00:14:00,465 --> 00:14:02,467
Youjin made porridge and took it to her.

177
00:14:04,427 --> 00:14:06,262
[Yongseok] Hmm. I see.

178
00:14:06,888 --> 00:14:08,514
Did she see a doctor?

179
00:14:08,598 --> 00:14:11,434
That poor girl is away from home
all by herself, and she's sick?

180
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,478
[Youjin] Ah. It's just a cold.

181
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:17,023
She had the porridge and took her meds.
Now, she's all better.

182
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:00,608
-[Minjae] Hello.
-[Jihoon] Hey.

183
00:15:03,778 --> 00:15:05,321
Can we get another glass, please?

184
00:15:05,404 --> 00:15:07,490
-[staff] Oh. Got it.
-[Minjae] I don't need one.

185
00:15:08,407 --> 00:15:09,575
I quit drinking.

186
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:13,162
We don't need the glass, actually.

187
00:15:13,246 --> 00:15:14,247
[staff] Got it.

188
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,297
You said you had a favor to ask me?

189
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:27,635
If it's something
I can help you with, I will.

190
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:30,763
If I can't, well,
there's not much I can do about that.

191
00:15:31,556 --> 00:15:34,600
But I came out here
to at least hear you out.

192
00:15:36,477 --> 00:15:38,604
I wanted to ask you a favor about Youjin.

193
00:15:41,566 --> 00:15:42,567
What about Youjin?

194
00:15:46,612 --> 00:15:47,613
[Jihoon] Uh...

195
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:51,993
This is Youjin's.

196
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:54,871
They're matching rings.

197
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:57,623
I can't keep them forever,

198
00:15:58,875 --> 00:16:00,835
so I'd like you to give them to her.

199
00:16:02,837 --> 00:16:04,589
Well, don't get me wrong.

200
00:16:04,672 --> 00:16:07,049
They're not mine. They're Youjin's.

201
00:16:07,133 --> 00:16:08,885
She didn't give them to me.

202
00:16:10,469 --> 00:16:13,514
Well, she did give them to me,

203
00:16:13,598 --> 00:16:15,433
but she didn't mean it that way.

204
00:16:17,476 --> 00:16:19,729
I'm not explaining this very well.

205
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:27,653
If they're Youjin's,
why don't you give them to her yourself?

206
00:16:28,613 --> 00:16:32,283
I can't. I can't call her right now.

207
00:16:33,367 --> 00:16:35,161
[Minjae] What do you mean,
you can't call her?

208
00:16:35,244 --> 00:16:37,955
She hasn't changed her number or anything.
Just call her.

209
00:16:38,039 --> 00:16:40,625
I don't need to explain
every little detail to you.

210
00:16:40,708 --> 00:16:42,835
No, I'm not asking you
to explain it to me.

211
00:16:43,711 --> 00:16:45,254
Just do it yourself.

212
00:16:48,758 --> 00:16:50,468
They're yours.

213
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:55,181
Youjin bought them for your birthday.

214
00:16:57,558 --> 00:17:00,561
You're supposed to hear this from her,

215
00:17:00,645 --> 00:17:03,064
but I'm telling you
because I think you misunderstand.

216
00:17:04,732 --> 00:17:06,359
What do you mean, misunderstand?

217
00:17:06,859 --> 00:17:09,028
That's... not what it is.

218
00:17:09,111 --> 00:17:11,239
Yeah, there's nothing
to misunderstand, really.

219
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:13,658
You know better than anyone

220
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:17,870
how Youjin feels
and how much she likes you.

221
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:24,168
So do better, you jerk.

222
00:17:25,711 --> 00:17:29,715
The timing, reality, the circumstances...
That's all just excuses and bullshit.

223
00:17:29,799 --> 00:17:30,841
[Minjae] It's not bullshit--

224
00:17:30,925 --> 00:17:32,301
It is, you jerk.

225
00:17:32,927 --> 00:17:35,763
Everything you're saying
is about making sure you'll be loved.

226
00:17:36,973 --> 00:17:41,102
If the circumstances are right,
if there's time, and if things are easier,

227
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:45,565
then she'll love you, you'll be loved,
and she won't leave.

228
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:46,983
That's your logic.

229
00:17:50,444 --> 00:17:51,779
Look, forget all that.

230
00:17:53,197 --> 00:17:55,533
Think about how you can love her instead.

231
00:17:57,702 --> 00:17:59,161
It's not hard. It's easy.

232
00:18:00,204 --> 00:18:03,666
Don't underestimate how she feels,
don't dismiss her feelings.

233
00:18:05,835 --> 00:18:07,128
Be sincere with her.

234
00:18:08,129 --> 00:18:10,172
Do the things she wants you to do,

235
00:18:10,256 --> 00:18:13,467
and don't do the things
she tells you she doesn't like.

236
00:18:15,136 --> 00:18:19,724
And if you don't know what she likes
or doesn't like, just ask her.

237
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:22,602
Ask her, and then just do that.

238
00:18:25,855 --> 00:18:27,732
Do you get what I'm saying?

239
00:18:32,028 --> 00:18:34,947
Jeez. Did you get it or what?

240
00:18:35,656 --> 00:18:38,200
[tuts] Why are there
so many students like you here?

241
00:18:39,660 --> 00:18:41,746
Jeez, it's like talking to a monkey.

242
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:43,748
[Minjae] What?

243
00:18:45,166 --> 00:18:47,960
Actually, you're tall, so...

244
00:18:48,044 --> 00:18:49,378
You're a chimpanzee.

245
00:18:54,634 --> 00:18:55,635
[Jihoon] I'm tired.

246
00:18:56,302 --> 00:18:57,678
[grunts] Let's go.

247
00:19:04,477 --> 00:19:05,770
Take that with you.

248
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:07,355
We're going to pay now.

249
00:19:21,327 --> 00:19:24,705
All right. You said you quit drinking,

250
00:19:24,789 --> 00:19:27,708
so next time,
let's grab some food instead of drinks.

251
00:19:28,209 --> 00:19:30,544
Sure. Next time, it'll be on me.

252
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:35,508
[Jihoon] Don't you have gloves?

253
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:37,468
Gloves?

254
00:19:38,761 --> 00:19:42,223
I lose stuff easily

255
00:19:42,306 --> 00:19:44,475
and they're uncomfortable,
so I don't wear them.

256
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:49,021
Look.

257
00:19:50,189 --> 00:19:54,568
Youjin knitted these herself

258
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:57,196
and gave them to me for Christmas.

259
00:19:59,824 --> 00:20:00,825
[Minjae] Ah.

260
00:20:01,534 --> 00:20:02,535
[Jihoon] Now go.

261
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:06,766
I know I'm the woman here,
but I'm going to put my pride aside

262
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:09,852
and make the first move.

263
00:21:11,353 --> 00:21:12,605
Park Minjae...

264
00:21:14,982 --> 00:21:15,983
I like you.

265
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:19,779
I want you to be my boyfriend.

266
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:53,479
[Youjin] Mom, can you hurry
and get mine ready first?

267
00:21:53,562 --> 00:21:54,688
[Miyoung] Yeah, I'm almost done.

268
00:21:54,772 --> 00:21:56,440
[Youjin] Okay. I'm not going to eat much.

269
00:21:56,524 --> 00:21:57,733
-Just a little.
-[Miyoung] All right.

270
00:21:58,567 --> 00:22:00,486
-I'm running late. Can you please...
-[Miyoung] Fine.

271
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:02,822
Hey, don't worry. You can take your time.

272
00:22:02,905 --> 00:22:04,865
Your brother is going
to drive you to school.

273
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:07,034
[Youjin] Huh?

274
00:22:21,048 --> 00:22:22,049
[Youseong] You sit in the back.

275
00:22:22,132 --> 00:22:23,133
[Youjin] Why?

276
00:22:23,217 --> 00:22:24,718
Because you get out before Subin.

277
00:22:25,469 --> 00:22:26,470
[Youjin] What?

278
00:22:58,711 --> 00:23:00,004
[Youseong] Subin, get in here.

279
00:23:01,422 --> 00:23:02,882
[Youjin] No, get in here.

280
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:04,884
[Youseong] No, here...

281
00:23:04,967 --> 00:23:06,051
-[Youjin] Come on, here.
-[Subin] Okay.

282
00:23:06,135 --> 00:23:07,136
[Youseong] Get in... here.

283
00:23:08,470 --> 00:23:09,889
[Subin] Hello.

284
00:23:09,972 --> 00:23:11,473
Yeah, hello, Subin.

285
00:23:18,689 --> 00:23:21,859
You didn't have to give me a ride, though.

286
00:23:21,942 --> 00:23:23,235
I would've been fine.

287
00:23:23,319 --> 00:23:24,403
[Youjin] Hmm.

288
00:23:24,486 --> 00:23:27,615
I'm already driving Youjin anyway,
so you might as well come with us.

289
00:23:28,657 --> 00:23:31,035
It's nice having someone
to chat with on the way.

290
00:23:32,703 --> 00:23:35,080
[Youseong] Right.
I heard you were sick, Subin.

291
00:23:36,332 --> 00:23:38,167
[Subin] Ah. Yeah.

292
00:23:38,876 --> 00:23:40,794
What about the doctor? Did you go see one?

293
00:23:41,503 --> 00:23:45,424
It wasn't that bad. It was just a cold.

294
00:23:45,507 --> 00:23:47,259
It's been so cold lately, so...

295
00:23:47,343 --> 00:23:48,344
[Youjin] Yeah.

296
00:23:48,427 --> 00:23:49,511
So I caught a cold.

297
00:23:49,595 --> 00:23:50,596
Right.

298
00:23:50,679 --> 00:23:53,349
[Youseong] I know.
It's been freezing the past few days.

299
00:23:53,432 --> 00:23:56,894
Too bad you got sick,
because it's supposed to stay cold.

300
00:23:58,729 --> 00:24:01,899
How about I keep giving you rides
until you're feeling better?

301
00:24:02,483 --> 00:24:04,944
Uh... No, I'm fine.

302
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:08,656
[Youseong] Well, I can just
pick you up too when I give Youjin a ride.

303
00:24:08,739 --> 00:24:11,492
[Youjin] Really? Dude, you're going
to give me a ride every morning?

304
00:24:11,992 --> 00:24:13,786
"Dude"? Show your brother some respect.

305
00:24:14,453 --> 00:24:16,038
Uh, I mean, sorry.

306
00:24:16,830 --> 00:24:18,999
So you're going
to give me a ride every morning?

307
00:24:19,083 --> 00:24:21,752
Well, it's cold,
and taking the bus can be exhausting.

308
00:24:21,835 --> 00:24:24,338
Mmm... Well, I'd love that.

309
00:24:26,966 --> 00:24:28,634
Subin, I can give you a ride too.

310
00:24:29,301 --> 00:24:31,261
Oh. Really?

311
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:36,433
You'll really give us a ride
every morning? You promise?

312
00:24:37,393 --> 00:24:39,436
Yay, I get to sleep an extra 30 minutes.

313
00:24:42,022 --> 00:24:45,109
Subin, do you have a boyfriend?

314
00:24:45,192 --> 00:24:47,528
-Sorry?
-Why would you ask something like that?

315
00:24:48,028 --> 00:24:49,780
[Youseong] Why not?
What's wrong with asking?

316
00:24:49,863 --> 00:24:53,367
I was just checking to find a nice guy
among my friends to set her up with.

317
00:24:53,450 --> 00:24:56,412
You don't have any nice guy friends.

318
00:24:57,121 --> 00:24:59,748
And you have no idea how popular Subin is.

319
00:24:59,832 --> 00:25:01,792
There are tons of guys lining up for her.

320
00:25:01,875 --> 00:25:03,210
No way.

321
00:25:03,293 --> 00:25:05,754
Who likes me? There's no one like that.

322
00:25:07,089 --> 00:25:10,467
Kim Sejin. He follows you around
because he likes you.

323
00:25:11,135 --> 00:25:12,136
[Youseong] Kim Sejin?

324
00:25:13,053 --> 00:25:14,304
Who's Kim Sejin?

325
00:25:14,388 --> 00:25:16,473
He's a guy from my cohort in the lab.

326
00:25:16,557 --> 00:25:19,685
He's smart, but kind of a jerk.

327
00:25:19,768 --> 00:25:21,812
Hmm. There's a guy like that?

328
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:24,106
No, he doesn't like me.

329
00:25:24,898 --> 00:25:26,817
And I don't like him either.

330
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:30,404
No, I didn't say you liked him.
I said he likes you.

331
00:25:30,988 --> 00:25:32,531
Yeah, I know.

332
00:25:32,614 --> 00:25:34,575
He doesn't like me, either.

333
00:25:36,035 --> 00:25:39,288
Anyway, there's nothing going on
between you two, right?

334
00:25:41,248 --> 00:25:42,624
No.

335
00:25:42,708 --> 00:25:44,543
Nothing.

336
00:25:44,626 --> 00:25:46,837
There's absolutely nothing between us.

337
00:25:48,964 --> 00:25:51,967
If you have any nice friends,
please set me up with one of them.

338
00:25:52,676 --> 00:25:53,802
Really?

339
00:25:54,762 --> 00:25:56,388
Should I set you up with my friend?

340
00:25:57,473 --> 00:25:58,932
Then how about a blind date?

341
00:26:00,142 --> 00:26:03,270
Apparently, my relative knows this guy
who is a MOFE deputy director.

342
00:26:03,353 --> 00:26:06,273
He went to our school,
and I hear he's a really great guy.

343
00:26:06,356 --> 00:26:09,443
Hey, Lim Youjin, don't butt in.
You stay out of this.

344
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:33,425
[Youjin] Oh, boy. Drive home safe. Bye.

345
00:26:41,141 --> 00:26:42,935
Hey. Kim Sejin.

346
00:26:56,657 --> 00:26:57,699
Look, Youjin.

347
00:27:00,911 --> 00:27:06,542
I didn't mean to put you
in a tough situation or anything.

348
00:27:06,625 --> 00:27:08,418
So don't get the wrong idea.

349
00:27:09,545 --> 00:27:10,838
[Youjin] The wrong idea?

350
00:27:10,921 --> 00:27:12,172
But you know what they say.

351
00:27:13,465 --> 00:27:16,009
"You make the mess, you clean it up."

352
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:18,887
Yeah, I do.

353
00:27:18,971 --> 00:27:21,140
You think I wouldn't know that saying?

354
00:27:21,223 --> 00:27:22,224
It's not that.

355
00:27:24,476 --> 00:27:25,978
Anyway, I... [clearing throat]

356
00:27:26,728 --> 00:27:31,441
[inhales] I believe the one who caused
the problem should be the one to fix it.

357
00:27:33,735 --> 00:27:35,487
So you need to...

358
00:27:37,114 --> 00:27:38,407
deal with your problem.

359
00:27:39,950 --> 00:27:41,702
What are you talking about?

360
00:27:43,787 --> 00:27:44,913
You'll know soon enough.

361
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:54,047
By the way, wasn't it...
Subin in the car just now?

362
00:27:55,632 --> 00:27:56,633
Yeah, it was.

363
00:27:56,717 --> 00:27:58,969
I forgot to reach out to her.

364
00:28:02,180 --> 00:28:04,474
Hey, didn't you two have a thing going on?

365
00:28:06,727 --> 00:28:07,978
There's nothing going on.

366
00:28:08,061 --> 00:28:10,314
We're just friends. Just friends.

367
00:28:10,397 --> 00:28:11,899
[Youjin] I see.

368
00:28:11,982 --> 00:28:14,276
Subin said there's nothing
between you two, either.

369
00:28:15,110 --> 00:28:17,654
That's what Subin said?
That there's nothing between us?

370
00:28:17,738 --> 00:28:18,739
[Youjin] Yeah.

371
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:21,450
And Subin is going on a blind date.

372
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:24,161
What?

373
00:28:24,953 --> 00:28:28,165
Well, we know this guy
who is a deputy director at the MOFE.

374
00:28:28,248 --> 00:28:30,834
And when I offered to set them up,
she said yes.

375
00:28:39,968 --> 00:28:40,969
[sighing] Damn it.

376
00:28:45,766 --> 00:28:47,976
[Sejin] <i>Subin, are you going</i>
<i>on a blind date?</i>

377
00:28:49,686 --> 00:28:50,687
YES

378
00:28:50,771 --> 00:28:51,772
SEND

379
00:28:52,439 --> 00:28:53,440
[Subin] <i>Yes.</i>

380
00:29:01,156 --> 00:29:02,449
[Sejin] <i>Why?</i>

381
00:29:03,867 --> 00:29:06,078
[mumbles] What does he mean, "Why?"

382
00:29:11,959 --> 00:29:13,669
<i>It's none of your business, isn't it?</i>

383
00:29:29,184 --> 00:29:30,769
INCOMING CALL
KIM SEJIN

384
00:29:33,188 --> 00:29:34,606
Aren't you going to answer that?

385
00:29:40,988 --> 00:29:42,155
It's a spam call.

386
00:29:43,824 --> 00:29:45,534
POWER OFF

387
00:29:47,619 --> 00:29:48,787
[automation]<i> The phone is turned off.</i>

388
00:29:48,870 --> 00:29:51,206
<i>You will now be connected to voicemail...</i>

389
00:30:19,234 --> 00:30:20,902
[Sejin] I'm going to head out.

390
00:30:20,986 --> 00:30:22,029
[Taeho] Huh?

391
00:30:22,112 --> 00:30:23,363
Are you going somewhere?

392
00:30:23,864 --> 00:30:25,741
[Sejin] Ah. Library. To the library.

393
00:30:25,824 --> 00:30:27,826
[Taeho] Hey, before you head off
to the library...

394
00:30:27,909 --> 00:30:29,911
-Hey, could you...
-[Hangyeol] Hey, where are you...

395
00:30:29,995 --> 00:30:31,621
No, I need to head out right now.

396
00:30:31,705 --> 00:30:34,374
-[Taeho] Hey! That little...
-[Hangyeol] But...

397
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:38,045
[Taeho] Hey.

398
00:30:39,629 --> 00:30:40,630
[Chansoo] Hey.

399
00:30:42,049 --> 00:30:43,050
Hey!

400
00:30:48,096 --> 00:30:49,097
[Hangyeol] Hey...

401
00:30:49,723 --> 00:30:50,891
Youjin.

402
00:30:50,974 --> 00:30:52,559
-[Youjin] Yes?
-[Hangyeol] Are you busy?

403
00:30:52,642 --> 00:30:54,352
-You're not? No?
-[Youjin] No.

404
00:30:54,436 --> 00:30:57,731
Well, I just have something to ask you.

405
00:30:57,814 --> 00:30:58,815
What?

406
00:30:59,232 --> 00:31:02,360
[Hangyeol] I don't know
if I should ask this, though.

407
00:31:04,071 --> 00:31:07,407
It's not really okay to pry
into someone's personal life, right?

408
00:31:07,991 --> 00:31:10,911
Mmm... Of course not.
Why would you even ask?

409
00:31:10,994 --> 00:31:13,080
Yeah, right? That's what I thought too.

410
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:16,333
[Chansoo] How is that personal?
It's a team matter.

411
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:17,542
It is personal.

412
00:31:17,626 --> 00:31:20,378
[groans] Enough, Hangyeol.
Forget it. [tuts]

413
00:31:22,255 --> 00:31:24,257
Youjin. So...

414
00:31:24,883 --> 00:31:27,552
Whether it's personal or not, I...

415
00:31:28,595 --> 00:31:33,308
Actually, even if it's personal,
I need to know this.

416
00:31:34,309 --> 00:31:35,310
Excuse me?

417
00:31:35,393 --> 00:31:37,896
Is it true that you and Minjae
used to date?

418
00:31:40,524 --> 00:31:45,320
I need to know the truth
so I know how to handle this.

419
00:31:47,697 --> 00:31:50,575
Is it true or not? Just tell me that.
Give me a straight answer.

420
00:31:56,998 --> 00:31:59,042
-Right. Answer the phone first.
-[Youjin] Uh...

421
00:32:02,129 --> 00:32:03,255
Yes. Hello?

422
00:32:05,298 --> 00:32:07,050
Yes, Professor. This is Youjin.

423
00:32:08,260 --> 00:32:09,261
What?

424
00:32:11,263 --> 00:32:12,264
Right now?

425
00:32:17,519 --> 00:32:18,520
[Jaehong] Yes.

426
00:32:25,861 --> 00:32:27,737
Have a seat. Mmm.

427
00:32:28,947 --> 00:32:33,451
So I asked to see you
because I wanted to ask you something.

428
00:32:35,662 --> 00:32:38,415
I'm not good at beating around the bush,
so I'll be straight.

429
00:32:39,708 --> 00:32:41,668
I hear you and Minjae used to date.

430
00:32:44,754 --> 00:32:45,755
Is it true?

431
00:32:49,134 --> 00:32:53,221
Did you two date in secret and break up
while Minjae was doing his postdoc abroad?

432
00:32:55,432 --> 00:32:57,684
Well, I'm not trying to pry

433
00:32:58,518 --> 00:33:01,438
into your personal life just to gossip.

434
00:33:02,480 --> 00:33:05,567
I'm asking because
it could cause problems in our lab.

435
00:33:05,650 --> 00:33:08,737
We didn't do anything
that could be problematic for the lab.

436
00:33:09,487 --> 00:33:11,615
So it's true that you two used to date?

437
00:33:12,365 --> 00:33:15,911
Yes, we used to date, but we didn't do
anything that could be problematic.

438
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:17,495
Dating in the lab...

439
00:33:19,539 --> 00:33:24,419
when you're supposed to be studying
is problematic in itself.

440
00:33:27,130 --> 00:33:29,966
If you're going to date,
do it right and get married.

441
00:33:31,343 --> 00:33:34,346
But no. You broke up, you fought,

442
00:33:34,429 --> 00:33:37,390
you vomited blood, and you ended up
in the hospital. I mean...

443
00:33:39,643 --> 00:33:40,727
What is this?

444
00:33:42,437 --> 00:33:44,773
Isn't all that
disrupting the academic environment

445
00:33:44,856 --> 00:33:46,483
and bringing down the whole lab?

446
00:33:50,445 --> 00:33:53,114
Of course, I'm not saying
this is all your fault.

447
00:33:53,198 --> 00:33:57,077
It takes two to tango, as they say.
Minjae was in the wrong, too.

448
00:33:57,160 --> 00:34:01,456
He's older, and as your senior,
he should've known better.

449
00:34:03,333 --> 00:34:05,168
That said... [smacks lips]

450
00:34:07,087 --> 00:34:10,340
You see, it'd be easier for you to move

451
00:34:11,716 --> 00:34:13,176
than Minjae.

452
00:34:13,843 --> 00:34:16,012
You've got less weighing you down.

453
00:34:17,764 --> 00:34:18,765
Pardon?

454
00:34:20,058 --> 00:34:21,101
Move?

455
00:34:21,184 --> 00:34:23,144
[smacks lips] You're almost done
with your master's,

456
00:34:23,228 --> 00:34:25,397
so you can finish it here.

457
00:34:26,856 --> 00:34:29,401
But after that,
consider transferring to another school.

458
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:34,281
[scoffs] But I didn't do anything
bad enough to get kicked out of school.

459
00:34:34,364 --> 00:34:35,949
No, you're not getting kicked out.

460
00:34:36,616 --> 00:34:38,868
I'll write you
the recommendation letters and all.

461
00:34:38,952 --> 00:34:40,412
What... No.

462
00:34:42,330 --> 00:34:45,375
[sighs] Then I'd rather
you make this an official matter

463
00:34:45,458 --> 00:34:47,377
and determine who's right and who's wrong.

464
00:34:48,920 --> 00:34:52,674
I'll take responsibility for my wrongs,
and accept any punishment from the school.

465
00:34:52,757 --> 00:34:54,384
That would be going too far.

466
00:34:55,343 --> 00:34:57,596
No, I don't think that's necessary.

467
00:34:57,679 --> 00:35:00,056
Yes, I do think it's necessary.

468
00:35:00,140 --> 00:35:02,434
I'll make this official
and take the punishment.

469
00:35:03,018 --> 00:35:05,186
[Jaehong] No, I mean... Youjin.

470
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:07,272
This isn't the US.

471
00:35:07,772 --> 00:35:10,734
It'll be awkward for two exes
to be around each other.

472
00:35:10,817 --> 00:35:12,277
The whole idea was just...

473
00:35:13,361 --> 00:35:15,905
that one of you
could be considerate of the other.

474
00:35:16,948 --> 00:35:19,826
Exactly. Why should I be the one
to be considerate?

475
00:35:19,909 --> 00:35:21,161
It's not awkward for me.

476
00:35:21,244 --> 00:35:23,371
Well, Minjae vomited blood.

477
00:35:25,832 --> 00:35:27,917
I'm asking for your sympathy. You...

478
00:35:28,501 --> 00:35:30,670
[exhales] Youjin, you...

479
00:35:33,632 --> 00:35:36,426
Don't you feel bad for Minjae?

480
00:35:37,761 --> 00:35:40,138
No, I don't feel bad for him at all.

481
00:35:40,221 --> 00:35:41,306
Oh, really?

482
00:35:43,308 --> 00:35:46,102
All right, then.
Let's ask Minjae to leave.

483
00:35:46,186 --> 00:35:49,272
Would that make you feel better?
Would you really be okay with that?

484
00:35:52,233 --> 00:35:53,568
I'm saying,

485
00:35:54,986 --> 00:35:56,279
you're a nice person,

486
00:35:58,073 --> 00:36:00,575
so you should give a little.

487
00:36:01,242 --> 00:36:04,871
[scoffs] I'm not nice. And actually...

488
00:36:07,415 --> 00:36:10,585
Minjae said he'd quit school anyway.

489
00:36:11,378 --> 00:36:12,462
What?

490
00:36:12,545 --> 00:36:15,048
He said he's quitting school
and quitting robotics, too.

491
00:36:15,131 --> 00:36:17,300
He's going to Canada or Toronto
or wherever.

492
00:36:17,842 --> 00:36:21,596
He's quitting school and robotics
because he got dumped by a woman?

493
00:36:22,263 --> 00:36:23,848
This bastard's lost his mind.

494
00:36:25,934 --> 00:36:28,812
When you date someone, you can get dumped.

495
00:36:28,895 --> 00:36:30,730
Has he ever even been in a relationship?

496
00:36:33,483 --> 00:36:35,443
Did he seriously say that?

497
00:36:35,527 --> 00:36:37,153
That he's going to quit school?

498
00:36:37,237 --> 00:36:38,697
[Youjin] You should ask him yourself.

499
00:36:40,573 --> 00:36:41,866
[Jaehong] What a crazy bastard.

500
00:36:43,952 --> 00:36:46,955
[doctor] You haven't vomited blood
since then, have you?

501
00:36:47,038 --> 00:36:48,039
No.

502
00:36:48,123 --> 00:36:49,541
GASTROENTEROLOGIST
JEONG YEONGJU

503
00:36:49,624 --> 00:36:52,585
And no black or red stools?
No abdominal pain?

504
00:36:52,669 --> 00:36:53,670
[Minjae] No.

505
00:36:53,753 --> 00:36:55,922
And no dizziness or anything?

506
00:36:56,005 --> 00:36:57,006
No.

507
00:36:57,507 --> 00:36:59,884
[doctor] But you have a slight fever.

508
00:36:59,968 --> 00:37:01,511
Yes, I have a bit of a fever.

509
00:37:01,594 --> 00:37:04,139
[doctor] Mmm...
And you've been feeling fatigued overall.

510
00:37:04,222 --> 00:37:05,223
Yes.

511
00:37:05,306 --> 00:37:07,142
[doctor] Looks like you've lost
some weight, too?

512
00:37:08,101 --> 00:37:11,604
I've only been eating porridge lately,
so that's probably why.

513
00:37:11,688 --> 00:37:12,814
[doctor] Mmm...

514
00:37:15,108 --> 00:37:18,278
Uh, do you have a cough or any phlegm?

515
00:37:18,737 --> 00:37:22,031
[Minjae] Mmm...
No, I don't think I have a cough.

516
00:37:22,615 --> 00:37:23,867
[doctor] Hmm...

517
00:37:25,660 --> 00:37:28,413
Could you lift your shirt up a little?

518
00:37:34,252 --> 00:37:35,253
All right.

519
00:37:36,629 --> 00:37:37,797
Breathe in.

520
00:37:39,758 --> 00:37:41,259
Slowly breathe out.

521
00:37:43,094 --> 00:37:46,306
-[doctor] And breathe in again.
-[Minjae inhales]

522
00:37:47,682 --> 00:37:49,934
-[doctor] And breathe out.
-[Minjae exhales]

523
00:37:53,354 --> 00:37:55,440
[doctor] Let's get a chest X-ray.

524
00:37:56,316 --> 00:37:58,902
But I don't have a cough. Why an X-ray?

525
00:37:58,985 --> 00:38:01,905
[doctor] Yeah. Just to take a look
and make sure everything's okay.

526
00:38:06,242 --> 00:38:09,078
[staff] Breathe in
and hold your breath for a moment.

527
00:38:12,165 --> 00:38:14,626
All right, done. You can breathe now.

528
00:38:14,709 --> 00:38:16,586
-You can leave the room now.
-[Minjae] Okay.

529
00:38:16,669 --> 00:38:18,671
X-RAY ROOM

530
00:38:54,374 --> 00:38:56,376
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY

531
00:39:24,028 --> 00:39:25,655
What are you doing here?

532
00:39:25,738 --> 00:39:29,659
Uh, I told you earlier
I'd be waiting here.

533
00:39:29,742 --> 00:39:32,370
[Subin] I told you
I didn't know when I'd finish.

534
00:39:34,747 --> 00:39:38,418
You said you didn't know
when you'd finish, but it'd be late.

535
00:39:38,501 --> 00:39:41,212
So I could either wait or not,
or just do whatever I wanted.

536
00:39:41,296 --> 00:39:43,715
-So I've been waiting--
-When I said you could either...

537
00:39:44,799 --> 00:39:48,177
[sighs] That's not what I meant.

538
00:39:48,261 --> 00:39:49,262
[Sejin] Oh.

539
00:39:50,805 --> 00:39:53,892
It seems I misunderstood.

540
00:39:55,310 --> 00:39:56,352
I'm sorry.

541
00:40:02,901 --> 00:40:06,237
So what did you want to say to me?

542
00:40:06,946 --> 00:40:08,114
Go ahead and say it.

543
00:40:08,781 --> 00:40:10,491
You said you wanted to say something.

544
00:40:11,075 --> 00:40:13,703
Why don't we go somewhere inside first...

545
00:40:13,786 --> 00:40:15,163
Have you eaten yet?

546
00:40:15,246 --> 00:40:17,665
[Subin] Yes, I had dinner earlier.

547
00:40:18,541 --> 00:40:19,542
[Sejin] Oh...

548
00:40:21,044 --> 00:40:24,005
What is it you wanted to say to me?
Just tell me here.

549
00:40:31,721 --> 00:40:34,599
I'm just curious...

550
00:40:36,434 --> 00:40:38,227
why you're going on a blind date.

551
00:40:39,145 --> 00:40:40,146
What?

552
00:40:43,358 --> 00:40:46,527
What do you mean, why? I'm just doing it.

553
00:40:47,362 --> 00:40:48,363
I mean,

554
00:40:49,572 --> 00:40:53,701
someone like you doesn't need
to go on blind dates.

555
00:40:53,785 --> 00:40:56,454
You could be with anyone you want.

556
00:40:56,537 --> 00:40:57,538
What?

557
00:40:58,247 --> 00:40:59,749
What does that even mean?

558
00:41:01,209 --> 00:41:04,170
Are you saying I'd date just anyone?

559
00:41:04,253 --> 00:41:06,297
[sighs] No, that's not what I mean.

560
00:41:15,848 --> 00:41:17,725
Honestly, I've...

561
00:41:20,728 --> 00:41:22,438
never met anyone

562
00:41:23,898 --> 00:41:25,817
as beautiful as you in my life.

563
00:41:28,403 --> 00:41:30,071
You're seriously the most beautiful person

564
00:41:31,197 --> 00:41:32,323
I've ever seen in my life.

565
00:41:34,325 --> 00:41:36,369
Celebrities, singers, idols...

566
00:41:37,370 --> 00:41:38,788
There are plenty of people
everyone says are beautiful,

567
00:41:40,164 --> 00:41:42,083
but honestly,
none of them even come close.

568
00:41:44,127 --> 00:41:47,046
I mean, if I'm being really generous here,

569
00:41:47,630 --> 00:41:50,008
sure, beauty is subjective,

570
00:41:50,091 --> 00:41:52,760
and everyone has their own type.

571
00:41:54,554 --> 00:41:57,056
But someone who's as smart, kind,

572
00:41:57,140 --> 00:41:59,684
considerate,
and compassionate as you are...

573
00:42:01,894 --> 00:42:04,063
Seriously, I swear on my life,

574
00:42:05,106 --> 00:42:06,482
there's no one else like that.

575
00:42:08,401 --> 00:42:10,611
So why would someone like you
go on a blind date?

576
00:42:12,071 --> 00:42:14,323
You don't need to do that.

577
00:42:15,450 --> 00:42:19,662
You could just pick anyone you like
and date them.

578
00:42:20,621 --> 00:42:22,832
I seriously don't understand
why you'd want to go

579
00:42:22,915 --> 00:42:24,834
meet some complete stranger like that.

580
00:42:34,385 --> 00:42:35,386
Do you...

581
00:42:37,138 --> 00:42:38,556
really think so?

582
00:42:39,140 --> 00:42:40,933
[voice breaking] Yes, I really think so.

583
00:42:42,185 --> 00:42:45,438
-[sniffles, sobs]
-[Subin sighs]

584
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:50,526
Then if...

585
00:42:52,278 --> 00:42:55,198
I said I wanted to date you, Sejin,
would you date me?

586
00:43:03,956 --> 00:43:06,667
What's wrong? You don't want to?

587
00:43:19,639 --> 00:43:20,640
I just...

588
00:43:24,435 --> 00:43:25,561
I feel like...

589
00:43:28,022 --> 00:43:29,273
my heart's going to burst...

590
00:43:32,110 --> 00:43:33,736
[chuckling] ...and I'm gonna die.

591
00:43:48,835 --> 00:43:50,670
-[Sejin sobs, chuckles]
-[Subin chuckles]

592
00:44:16,195 --> 00:44:18,489
You haven't eaten yet?
What have you been doing?

593
00:44:19,574 --> 00:44:21,159
I had so much to go over today.

594
00:44:21,242 --> 00:44:23,161
I was too busy to even think about eating.

595
00:44:23,244 --> 00:44:25,329
Even if you're busy, you can't skip meals.

596
00:44:27,248 --> 00:44:28,749
You should have some too.

597
00:44:28,833 --> 00:44:31,002
No, I've already eaten. I'm fine. Eat up.

598
00:44:31,502 --> 00:44:33,212
-Eat with me anyway.
-No.

599
00:44:34,589 --> 00:44:37,800
Is it still too soon to eat raw fish?

600
00:44:37,884 --> 00:44:38,885
Maybe you can't eat it yet?

601
00:44:44,682 --> 00:44:46,017
[Youjin] You went
to the hospital today, right?

602
00:44:46,100 --> 00:44:48,060
Did the doctor say you're okay now?

603
00:44:49,061 --> 00:44:50,062
[Minjae] Yeah.

604
00:44:50,897 --> 00:44:53,399
Come on, eat first.
I'll tell you when you're done.

605
00:44:57,069 --> 00:44:59,030
[chuckles softly] I'm done.

606
00:44:59,697 --> 00:45:00,698
I'm really done.

607
00:45:06,204 --> 00:45:09,999
-So, as for the endoscopy...
-[Youjin] Mmm-hmm.

608
00:45:11,792 --> 00:45:14,253
They said the bleeding's stopped
and it's healing well.

609
00:45:15,254 --> 00:45:16,422
That's great to hear.

610
00:45:19,508 --> 00:45:20,676
What's up?

611
00:45:20,760 --> 00:45:22,929
Is there something else?

612
00:45:23,012 --> 00:45:24,013
[Minjae] Hmm?

613
00:45:28,142 --> 00:45:30,895
Well, I have a bit of a fever.

614
00:45:31,479 --> 00:45:34,690
And since I've had surgery
for lung cancer before,

615
00:45:34,774 --> 00:45:36,359
they wanted to check a few things,

616
00:45:36,442 --> 00:45:38,903
and they wanted to do a chest X-ray.

617
00:45:39,904 --> 00:45:42,156
I see. So did you do it?

618
00:45:42,865 --> 00:45:43,866
Yeah. And...

619
00:45:44,867 --> 00:45:46,744
apparently, there's a nodule in my lung.

620
00:45:47,828 --> 00:45:49,080
They said they won't know

621
00:45:49,163 --> 00:45:52,291
if it's just a lump or cancer
until they do a biopsy.

622
00:45:53,167 --> 00:45:55,086
I'll get the results next week.

623
00:45:57,129 --> 00:45:58,506
I'm sure it isn't.

624
00:45:59,632 --> 00:46:03,052
Well, even if it's cancer,
you can get it treated.

625
00:46:04,595 --> 00:46:05,596
[Minjae] Yeah.

626
00:46:06,097 --> 00:46:07,098
[Youjin] Yeah.

627
00:46:09,725 --> 00:46:10,726
I'm sorry.

628
00:46:12,687 --> 00:46:14,313
Sorry for what?

629
00:46:14,397 --> 00:46:15,982
You didn't do anything wrong.

630
00:46:17,525 --> 00:46:20,319
I know. I didn't do anything wrong,
so why am I so unlucky?

631
00:46:24,115 --> 00:46:26,284
If I died now,

632
00:46:28,494 --> 00:46:30,496
I'd die without having
accomplished anything,

633
00:46:30,579 --> 00:46:31,998
with nothing to leave behind.

634
00:46:32,081 --> 00:46:33,916
God, it'd all feel so pointless.

635
00:46:35,501 --> 00:46:36,502
[Youjin] Yeah.

636
00:46:40,881 --> 00:46:44,135
[Minjae] What you said the other day.
Is it true?

637
00:46:45,761 --> 00:46:46,762
What?

638
00:46:47,763 --> 00:46:50,266
That you'd rather die
than break up with me?

639
00:46:52,560 --> 00:46:54,937
Yeah, I really meant it.

640
00:46:57,231 --> 00:47:00,067
Seriously, what are you
going to do if I die?

641
00:47:02,987 --> 00:47:04,697
[smacks lips] Then,

642
00:47:04,780 --> 00:47:06,741
-I'll die too.
-[Minjae chuckles softly]

643
00:47:15,249 --> 00:47:16,667
I'm serious.

644
00:47:16,751 --> 00:47:18,711
I'm really going to die too.

645
00:47:18,794 --> 00:47:20,171
Come on. [chuckles dryly]

646
00:47:20,254 --> 00:47:21,547
Don't be ridiculous.

647
00:47:34,977 --> 00:47:35,978
I'm sorry.

648
00:47:36,479 --> 00:47:37,772
-Hey, I'm sorry. That was wrong.
-[Youjin sobs]

649
00:47:37,855 --> 00:47:40,691
Come here. Come. Don't cry.

650
00:47:40,775 --> 00:47:44,653
I'm sorry. Okay? I'm sorry.

651
00:47:59,543 --> 00:48:03,798
But don't hate me, okay? Okay?

652
00:48:04,340 --> 00:48:05,841
-[Youjin sniffles]
-[Minjae] Don't hate me.

653
00:48:07,093 --> 00:48:08,427
[Youjin] I don't hate you.

654
00:48:12,181 --> 00:48:13,557
I love you.

655
00:48:16,018 --> 00:48:17,436
I love you.

656
00:48:46,340 --> 00:48:47,633
[Youjin] What are you thinking about?

657
00:48:48,134 --> 00:48:49,135
[Minjae] Hmm?

658
00:48:50,845 --> 00:48:52,930
Why do you keep looking elsewhere
when I'm right here by your side?

659
00:48:54,056 --> 00:48:55,307
Look at me.

660
00:49:00,688 --> 00:49:02,773
I'm going with you
to the hospital on Tuesday.

661
00:49:04,358 --> 00:49:05,609
Aren't you going to work?

662
00:49:05,693 --> 00:49:07,570
No, I can take the afternoon off.

663
00:49:10,030 --> 00:49:12,741
No, you don't need to come.
I'll just call you.

664
00:49:13,868 --> 00:49:16,036
No, I'm going to go with you.

665
00:49:16,120 --> 00:49:17,872
I'd worry too much if you went alone.

666
00:49:21,500 --> 00:49:22,751
That's our taxi, right?

667
00:49:23,752 --> 00:49:24,795
[Minjae] Yeah, it is.

668
00:49:32,261 --> 00:49:33,262
Aren't you coming?

669
00:49:33,345 --> 00:49:34,346
[Minjae] Youjin.

670
00:49:36,474 --> 00:49:37,683
I think this is it for us.

671
00:49:42,104 --> 00:49:44,607
I really regretted hurting you back then.

672
00:49:46,317 --> 00:49:48,944
Then I promised myself
I'd be really good to you.

673
00:49:49,778 --> 00:49:52,031
But I guess we were meant to be this way.

674
00:49:52,114 --> 00:49:53,365
There's nothing to be done.

675
00:49:55,743 --> 00:49:57,203
Still, I'm glad that we at least

676
00:49:57,286 --> 00:50:00,039
get to say goodbye
face-to-face this time. Right?

677
00:50:00,122 --> 00:50:02,750
Come on. Why are you doing this again?

678
00:50:02,833 --> 00:50:03,834
I...

679
00:50:05,002 --> 00:50:06,921
don't deserve to be with you.

680
00:50:07,004 --> 00:50:08,130
I have no right to be.

681
00:50:10,424 --> 00:50:12,885
Who gets to decide
if you have the right to be with me?

682
00:50:12,968 --> 00:50:16,388
It's not God. It's not Buddha. It's me.

683
00:50:16,472 --> 00:50:17,890
I gave you that right.

684
00:50:17,973 --> 00:50:20,309
Just like me. I said you could love me.

685
00:50:21,018 --> 00:50:23,145
I get why you're doing this,

686
00:50:23,229 --> 00:50:25,272
but maybe the results
will show it's nothing.

687
00:50:25,356 --> 00:50:27,816
And if it really is cancer,
then we'll get it treated.

688
00:50:27,900 --> 00:50:28,984
I'll be with you. Okay?

689
00:50:29,068 --> 00:50:32,112
Yeah, well, that's not as easy
as you think, okay?

690
00:50:32,905 --> 00:50:37,701
A devoted woman staying by the side
of some poor guy who's dying?

691
00:50:38,285 --> 00:50:40,788
That's the kind of thing
you see in novels and movies.

692
00:50:40,871 --> 00:50:44,124
It's easy to say you'll take care
of someone who's dying. But it's not.

693
00:50:46,502 --> 00:50:48,337
I decide whether it's easy or not.

694
00:50:48,420 --> 00:50:49,588
What if I die?

695
00:50:50,339 --> 00:50:53,217
What would happen then?
What would happen to you?

696
00:50:54,260 --> 00:50:57,471
Will you spend your whole life
looking back on all our happy memories?

697
00:50:57,555 --> 00:50:59,181
Crying every day?

698
00:50:59,265 --> 00:51:01,350
I told you, if you die, I'll die too.

699
00:51:01,433 --> 00:51:03,269
[yells] Don't be such a child!

700
00:51:03,352 --> 00:51:05,688
-You're not dying, okay? You...
-[Youjin sighs in frustration]

701
00:51:06,939 --> 00:51:08,691
Do you even know what it means to die?

702
00:51:10,776 --> 00:51:12,319
-God...
-Listen.

703
00:51:13,696 --> 00:51:17,366
Even if it's not me, you'll find someone
to spend the rest of your life with.

704
00:51:18,033 --> 00:51:21,579
So stop being so stubborn.
Stop acting like a child, for God's sake!

705
00:51:21,662 --> 00:51:23,414
And you stop lecturing me.

706
00:51:24,248 --> 00:51:26,750
Are you my mom? My dad?
Who are you to lecture me?

707
00:51:26,834 --> 00:51:29,753
You... I'm your senior.
So yes, I can lecture you.

708
00:51:29,837 --> 00:51:32,006
In the lab, yes,
but we're out in public now!

709
00:51:32,089 --> 00:51:33,299
Hey!

710
00:51:33,382 --> 00:51:34,675
[Youjin sighs] Okay, fine.

711
00:51:34,758 --> 00:51:36,343
[exhales] All right, fine.

712
00:51:37,177 --> 00:51:40,389
Let's wait for the results for now,
and then we'll talk, okay?

713
00:51:40,973 --> 00:51:42,933
If it's nothing, we're good.

714
00:51:43,017 --> 00:51:46,478
-If not, we'll talk again then. Okay?
-[taxi honks]

715
00:51:46,562 --> 00:51:50,733
Well... it won't make
any difference, okay?

716
00:51:50,816 --> 00:51:52,985
Even if I somehow get through this one,

717
00:51:53,068 --> 00:51:56,113
I'll have to go back in six months
and get tested all over again.

718
00:51:56,196 --> 00:51:57,448
[Youjin] Fine. Let's go for now--

719
00:51:57,531 --> 00:51:59,283
Then after those six months?

720
00:51:59,366 --> 00:52:01,410
-I get another six months.
-[Youjin sighs]

721
00:52:02,411 --> 00:52:05,914
And I'll still be wondering,
"When will it come back? When will I die?"

722
00:52:05,998 --> 00:52:08,709
I'll spend my whole life
on a razor's edge.

723
00:52:08,792 --> 00:52:12,588
That's the kind of miserable life
I'll have to live.

724
00:52:12,671 --> 00:52:14,965
Nothing's going to change. So...

725
00:52:16,550 --> 00:52:18,636
-[scoffs]
-[Minjae] Let's end this.

726
00:52:21,639 --> 00:52:23,307
I really want to stop doing this.

727
00:52:23,390 --> 00:52:25,392
This isn't some sacrifice
or act of devotion!

728
00:52:25,976 --> 00:52:30,898
I just need you in my life to be happy.
That's why...

729
00:52:30,981 --> 00:52:33,150
That's why I'm trying
and fighting for this.

730
00:52:34,735 --> 00:52:36,695
And you're acting
like you know what's best.

731
00:52:36,779 --> 00:52:38,864
You have all this courage
to break up with me,

732
00:52:38,947 --> 00:52:41,075
but you don't have the courage
to fight for me?

733
00:52:42,201 --> 00:52:44,703
God, not again.
How can you do this again...

734
00:52:46,080 --> 00:52:47,956
[groans] I can't believe
this is happening.

735
00:55:36,166 --> 00:55:37,251
[nurse] Mr. Park Minjae.

736
00:55:37,334 --> 00:55:38,335
[Minjae] Yes.

737
00:55:45,133 --> 00:55:46,343
[doctor] All right.

738
00:55:47,094 --> 00:55:48,470
If you look here,

739
00:55:48,554 --> 00:55:53,141
you can see two three-centimeter nodules
in the lung. Uh...

740
00:55:53,225 --> 00:55:54,601
So we did a biopsy, and...

741
00:55:54,685 --> 00:55:56,144
THORACIC SURGEON
SONG GIYEOL

742
00:55:56,228 --> 00:55:59,189
The results confirm
that they are cancerous.

743
00:56:01,775 --> 00:56:04,611
The squamous cell carcinoma has recurred.

744
00:56:06,446 --> 00:56:09,116
They're not that large, but...

745
00:56:09,199 --> 00:56:10,576
I do think you'll need surgery.

746
00:56:11,952 --> 00:56:14,871
The concern is that
this is the site of the recurrence,

747
00:56:14,955 --> 00:56:17,583
and it seems the cancer
has already started to spread.

748
00:56:17,666 --> 00:56:19,918
So we'll need to perform
open-chest surgery

749
00:56:20,002 --> 00:56:22,963
and remove the entire
lower lobe of your left lung.

750
00:56:23,046 --> 00:56:25,340
Doctor, it's not
a difficult surgery, is it?

751
00:56:25,424 --> 00:56:26,425
That's...

752
00:56:26,508 --> 00:56:28,635
The surgery will remove
all the cancer, right?

753
00:56:28,719 --> 00:56:30,429
He'll be okay after that, right?

754
00:56:30,512 --> 00:56:33,765
[Giyeol] Uh, well... Uh...

755
00:56:33,849 --> 00:56:36,184
When can he get the surgery?

756
00:56:36,768 --> 00:56:37,769
[Giyeol] Mmm.

757
00:56:38,353 --> 00:56:41,023
Well, let's see what we can schedule.

758
00:56:42,190 --> 00:56:44,026
Yeah. Okay.

759
00:57:14,431 --> 00:57:17,184
[automation] <i>The outer-circle train</i>

760
00:57:17,267 --> 00:57:21,021
<i>bound for Seongsu Station is now arriving.</i>

761
00:57:21,980 --> 00:57:25,984
<i>The doors are opening.</i>
<i>Please watch your step.</i>

762
00:57:26,068 --> 00:57:33,033
<i>Please watch your step.</i>

763
00:57:33,116 --> 00:57:40,082
<i>Please watch your step.</i>

764
00:59:03,832 --> 00:59:05,208
[Minjae] Do you want some strawberries?

765
00:59:13,842 --> 00:59:15,343
Which one do you think is better?

766
00:59:19,556 --> 00:59:20,891
Which one do you like better?

767
00:59:23,935 --> 00:59:25,187
-This one?
-[Minjae] This one?

768
01:00:37,092 --> 01:00:41,137
ARC LAB
RESEARCH ASSISTANT RECRUITMENT

769
01:00:41,221 --> 01:00:43,306
NO PRIOR EXPERIENCE OR KNOWLEDGE REQUIRED

770
01:00:43,390 --> 01:00:45,976
ASSISTANT PROFESSOR PARK MINJAE
OF MECHANICAL ENGINEERING

771
01:00:46,059 --> 01:00:49,688
[Minjae] All right, today, we're going to
continue from where we left off last time

772
01:00:49,771 --> 01:00:53,483
and take a closer look
at systems of linear equations.

773
01:00:54,234 --> 01:00:57,737
Now, the key to a system
of linear equations ultimately comes down

774
01:00:57,821 --> 01:01:01,324
to what constant values
B the unknowns X map to.

775
01:01:01,408 --> 01:01:05,245
If all the constants
on the right-hand side are zero,

776
01:01:05,328 --> 01:01:08,623
we call it a homogeneous system, right?

777
01:01:10,041 --> 01:01:13,378
In that case, we're always guaranteed
to have the trivial solution,

778
01:01:13,461 --> 01:01:15,797
where all the unknowns are zero.

779
01:01:15,881 --> 01:01:19,342
Well, I've met him,
and he seemed like a nice guy.

780
01:01:19,426 --> 01:01:20,969
Come on, he's fine.

781
01:01:22,971 --> 01:01:25,932
Try all you want, but parents can't win
against their own kids.

782
01:01:30,353 --> 01:01:32,647
What mother misses
the pre-wedding family meeting?

783
01:01:35,275 --> 01:01:38,236
Are you really going to meet
your son-in-law at the wedding?

784
01:01:43,366 --> 01:01:44,618
Are you really not coming?

785
01:01:51,416 --> 01:01:52,792
Suit yourself.

786
01:01:54,169 --> 01:01:56,046
Go ahead and break your daughter's heart.

787
01:02:03,970 --> 01:02:05,013
Mom's not coming?

788
01:02:05,555 --> 01:02:07,432
[Yongseok] Well, she says
she has a terrible headache

789
01:02:07,515 --> 01:02:08,642
and just can't make it.

790
01:02:09,351 --> 01:02:10,685
Her head hurts too much.

791
01:02:13,480 --> 01:02:15,023
Let's just go without her.

792
01:02:15,106 --> 01:02:16,566
Mom can join next time.

793
01:02:18,151 --> 01:02:19,152
Is that okay?

794
01:02:19,861 --> 01:02:21,821
Sure. There will be a next time.

795
01:02:21,905 --> 01:02:23,156
It's okay. Let's go.

796
01:03:14,958 --> 01:03:15,959
Gosh.

797
01:03:23,967 --> 01:03:25,510
[mumbling] Let's go.

798
01:03:25,593 --> 01:03:28,722
I'll just face it. I'll see.

799
01:03:29,514 --> 01:03:32,350
Yeah. We left early in case of traffic.

800
01:03:33,393 --> 01:03:34,602
Yeah, exactly.

801
01:03:36,104 --> 01:03:37,564
But my mom...

802
01:03:38,523 --> 01:03:40,984
Never mind. We'll talk when you're here.

803
01:03:41,067 --> 01:03:43,236
-[camera shutter clicks]
-Where are you? Are you almost here?

804
01:03:43,319 --> 01:03:46,322
Ah. I'm almost there.

805
01:03:46,406 --> 01:03:50,535
I should be there
in about five to ten minutes.

806
01:03:51,995 --> 01:03:53,329
Okay. Yeah.

807
01:03:54,581 --> 01:03:55,665
Bye.

808
01:03:59,002 --> 01:04:00,712
[staff] Here's the bouquet you ordered.

809
01:04:00,795 --> 01:04:03,423
Yes. Thank you.

810
01:04:03,506 --> 01:04:04,758
-Thank you.
-No problem.

811
01:04:04,841 --> 01:04:05,925
[Minjae] Bye.

812
01:04:55,016 --> 01:04:56,059
[Minjae] Oh, no.

813
01:04:57,102 --> 01:04:58,103
[Miyoung] Oh, my.

814
01:04:58,186 --> 01:04:59,187
Are you okay?

815
01:04:59,270 --> 01:05:00,271
[Miyoung] Yeah, I'm okay.

816
01:05:01,606 --> 01:05:03,316
-Thank you.
-No, not at all.

817
01:05:03,399 --> 01:05:05,235
-[Miyoung] Thank you so much.
-Are you really okay?

818
01:05:05,318 --> 01:05:06,736
[Miyoung] Yes, I'm okay.

819
01:05:06,820 --> 01:05:07,904
[Minjae] Okay.

820
01:05:07,987 --> 01:05:09,864
-[Miyoung gasps] Oh, no. I'm so sorry.
-[Minjae] No, don't worry.

821
01:05:09,948 --> 01:05:12,033
Hey, maybe we got here too early.

822
01:05:13,409 --> 01:05:15,203
It's better to be early than late.

823
01:05:16,329 --> 01:05:17,705
It's almost time.

824
01:05:32,887 --> 01:05:35,056
[Minjae] <i>Sorry.</i>
<i>I think I'll be about 10 minutes late.</i>

825
01:05:36,141 --> 01:05:39,018
-[chuckling] I'm sorry.
-No, I'm really fine. Are you okay?

826
01:05:39,102 --> 01:05:40,395
I'll pay for the flowers.

827
01:05:40,478 --> 01:05:42,605
-No. Seriously, no...
-No, seriously, let me pay.

828
01:05:42,689 --> 01:05:44,566
-It was my mistake.
-No, it was me.

829
01:05:47,819 --> 01:05:50,071
How tall are you, by the way?

830
01:05:50,155 --> 01:05:54,325
-My height? About 186 or 187, I think.
-[Miyoung gasps]

831
01:05:54,868 --> 01:05:56,452
Ah. [chuckles]

832
01:05:56,536 --> 01:05:59,205
My son is short.

833
01:05:59,289 --> 01:06:01,624
It's not like he didn't eat,
but he just didn't grow.

834
01:06:01,708 --> 01:06:03,960
-[Minjae] Oh.
-I'm so jealous. [chuckles]

835
01:06:06,713 --> 01:06:08,965
Well, just like the old folks used to say,

836
01:06:09,048 --> 01:06:13,136
-you're as handsome as paint.
-[staff chuckles]

837
01:06:13,219 --> 01:06:14,971
-Am I right? [chuckles]
-[staff] Yes. [chuckles]

838
01:06:15,054 --> 01:06:17,265
Thank you.

839
01:06:18,349 --> 01:06:19,350
[Miyoung] Mmm.

840
01:06:20,393 --> 01:06:21,769
-Ah...
-[Minjae] Yes?

841
01:06:21,853 --> 01:06:25,023
Since you're so tall and handsome,

842
01:06:25,106 --> 01:06:27,400
do you work as a model,
or work in show business?

843
01:06:27,483 --> 01:06:30,486
Oh, no, no. Nothing like that.

844
01:06:30,570 --> 01:06:33,198
I'm just teaching students,
kids at school.

845
01:06:33,698 --> 01:06:35,700
You're a teacher? [gasps]

846
01:06:35,783 --> 01:06:37,285
My goodness.

847
01:06:44,000 --> 01:06:45,627
There are guys like this out there,

848
01:06:45,710 --> 01:06:48,004
and why did she have to...

849
01:06:56,054 --> 01:06:58,306
My daughter is tall.

850
01:06:58,389 --> 01:07:00,475
-[Minjae] Oh...
-And pretty.

851
01:07:00,558 --> 01:07:03,770
She's pretty and smart.
She goes to Seohan National University.

852
01:07:03,853 --> 01:07:05,939
-[chuckles softly]

853
01:07:06,022 --> 01:07:07,690
Seohan National University?

854
01:07:08,942 --> 01:07:10,985
Yes. She's going to grad school there.

855
01:07:11,069 --> 01:07:14,530
She's doing a PhD
in mechanical engineering.

856
01:07:14,614 --> 01:07:16,866
She wants to become a professor.

857
01:07:20,119 --> 01:07:21,120
[Minjae] Oh.

858
01:07:24,290 --> 01:07:27,919
Do you have a girlfriend?
Are you in a relationship?

859
01:07:28,586 --> 01:07:31,798
-I do. Yes, I have a girlfriend.
-[Miyoung] Mmm.

860
01:07:33,007 --> 01:07:37,637
So these flowers must be for her, then.

861
01:07:37,720 --> 01:07:40,682
No, I bought those for her mother...

862
01:07:41,474 --> 01:07:42,475
Her mother?

863
01:07:42,558 --> 01:07:43,601
Yes.

864
01:07:43,685 --> 01:07:45,019
My goodness. [gasps]

865
01:07:48,314 --> 01:07:51,901
She's so lucky to have you
buying her things like this.

866
01:07:52,777 --> 01:07:53,778
[Minjae] Hmm...

867
01:07:54,320 --> 01:07:55,530
[staff] Your bouquet is ready.

868
01:07:55,613 --> 01:07:57,490
Okay. How much is it? I...

869
01:07:57,573 --> 01:07:59,117
Yes. That'll be 55,000 won.

870
01:07:59,200 --> 01:08:01,577
-[Miyoung] Let me...
-Are you, by any chance...

871
01:08:02,912 --> 01:08:04,789
Youjin's mother?

872
01:08:04,872 --> 01:08:07,959
Oh, my gosh!
How do you know my daughter's name?

873
01:08:09,168 --> 01:08:11,296
Hello, I'm Park Minjae.

874
01:08:11,379 --> 01:08:12,380
[Miyoung] What...

875
01:08:13,047 --> 01:08:15,133
Yes, I'm Park Minjae.

876
01:08:16,718 --> 01:08:17,885
Hello.

877
01:08:17,969 --> 01:08:20,096
Where are you? How far away are you?

878
01:08:24,392 --> 01:08:25,727
Right outside the restaurant?

879
01:08:25,810 --> 01:08:28,604
There. Yeah, come in.

880
01:08:36,654 --> 01:08:37,655
Hey, I'm here.

881
01:08:45,747 --> 01:08:46,748
[Youjin] Yeah, this way.

882
01:08:52,670 --> 01:08:53,671
[Minjae] Hello.

883
01:08:56,507 --> 01:08:58,009
Mom, you said you weren't coming.

884
01:08:59,427 --> 01:09:01,012
How did you two come together?

885
01:09:01,721 --> 01:09:04,307
Hello. We met in front of the restaurant.

886
01:09:04,390 --> 01:09:07,435
I didn't recognize her at first
because I'd never met her before.

887
01:09:07,518 --> 01:09:10,313
I was so surprised when I realized
it was her. Right, Ms. Seo?

888
01:09:18,696 --> 01:09:21,532
It turns out Youjin got her beauty
from her mother.

889
01:09:22,367 --> 01:09:24,160
That's how I recognized her right away.

890
01:09:26,079 --> 01:09:28,581
Ah. My mother will be here
in a minute too.

891
01:09:30,625 --> 01:09:32,710
He's polite and nice, isn't he?

892
01:09:33,378 --> 01:09:34,379
[whispering] I don't know.

893
01:09:35,963 --> 01:09:37,840
-[knock on door]
-[staff] Your guest is here.

894
01:09:37,924 --> 01:09:38,925
[Minjae] Okay.

895
01:09:40,468 --> 01:09:41,469
[Youseong and Yongseok] Oh.

896
01:09:42,303 --> 01:09:43,805
-[Youjin] Oh.
-[Minjae] You're here.

897
01:09:43,888 --> 01:09:44,889
-[Youseong] Hello.
-[Miyoung grunts]

898
01:09:47,183 --> 01:09:48,184
[Eunjoo] Let's sit.

899
01:09:51,437 --> 01:09:53,106
I'm sorry I'm late.

900
01:09:53,189 --> 01:09:55,733
I tried to get here sooner,
but traffic was terrible.

901
01:09:55,817 --> 01:09:58,444
Don't worry about it.
We just got here too.

902
01:10:00,363 --> 01:10:01,698
-[Minjae] All right. Let's sit.
-[Eunjoo] Okay.

903
01:10:01,781 --> 01:10:02,782
[Yongseok] Oh.

904
01:10:11,958 --> 01:10:13,793
This is my father.

905
01:10:14,585 --> 01:10:16,504
-[Eunjoo] Okay.
-Hello.

906
01:10:16,587 --> 01:10:18,131
I'm Youjin's father.

907
01:10:18,214 --> 01:10:19,674
Yes. Nice to meet you.

908
01:10:19,757 --> 01:10:22,218
-And this is my mother.
-Yes, hello.

909
01:10:22,969 --> 01:10:24,220
This is my brother.

910
01:10:24,303 --> 01:10:26,472
-Hello. I'm Youjin's brother.
-Nice to meet you.

911
01:10:32,478 --> 01:10:35,189
It's spring,
but it's still pretty chilly, isn't it?

912
01:10:35,273 --> 01:10:37,400
Should we order some hot tea first?

913
01:10:37,483 --> 01:10:38,484
Yes.

914
01:10:48,953 --> 01:10:52,582
By the way, have we met before?

915
01:10:52,665 --> 01:10:54,500
I feel like we've met before.

916
01:10:55,376 --> 01:10:58,671
I'm not sure.
This is my first time seeing you.

917
01:11:04,135 --> 01:11:05,219
-[Youjin tuts]
-[Minjae huffs]

918
01:11:05,303 --> 01:11:08,139
How could she lie like that
without even batting an eye?

919
01:11:09,182 --> 01:11:11,601
Well, I wouldn't call it lying.

920
01:11:11,684 --> 01:11:15,313
She was just pretending not to know,
given the situation.

921
01:11:15,396 --> 01:11:18,316
I mean, she could've just owned up to it
and apologized.

922
01:11:18,399 --> 01:11:19,525
Why'd she have to lie?

923
01:11:20,151 --> 01:11:22,528
Well, I said it's not lying.

924
01:11:23,571 --> 01:11:25,656
And you?

925
01:11:25,740 --> 01:11:28,242
You shouldn't talk
about your mother-in-law like that.

926
01:11:29,285 --> 01:11:31,245
Will you keep siding with her
instead of me?

927
01:11:32,413 --> 01:11:33,623
[chuckling] No.

928
01:11:34,874 --> 01:11:36,292
Sorry.

929
01:11:38,461 --> 01:11:39,587
You better behave.

930
01:11:40,213 --> 01:11:42,131
Okay. I will.

931
01:11:44,592 --> 01:11:47,345
[groans] I was so nervous. Now I'm tired.

932
01:11:49,055 --> 01:11:50,389
-Get some rest.
-[Youjin] Okay.

933
01:11:50,473 --> 01:11:51,516
Get some shut-eye.

934
01:11:51,599 --> 01:11:53,142
Let me close my eyes for a bit.

935
01:11:53,226 --> 01:11:54,227
[Minjae] Yeah.

936
01:12:09,283 --> 01:12:10,576
What are you thinking about?

937
01:12:13,788 --> 01:12:14,789
Me?

938
01:12:18,334 --> 01:12:19,669
About kissing you.

939
01:13:22,023 --> 01:13:25,943
BETWEEN STEPS

940
01:14:32,677 --> 01:14:37,181
AHN PANSUK

941
01:14:41,644 --> 01:14:45,648
THE END
